  "memory_before": {
    "meridian-credits/release-agreements": "Meridian Credits: supported release agreements (main.py RELEASE_AGREEMENTS / CURRENT_RELEASE).\n\nRelease \"1.0\" (original, still supported when explicitly requested):\n- credit = 10% of charge_cents, rounded down per line\n- cap = 2400 cents, shared per (account_id, subscription_id) group\n- priority within cap group: earliest service_on first, ties by increasing line_id\n\nRelease \"2.0\" (Finance permanently adopted as the CURRENT default as of trial-b2v, 2026-09-07):\n- credit = 15% of charge_cents, rounded down per line\n- cap = 3000 cents, shared per account_id (across all its subscriptions)\n- priority within cap group: largest charge_cents first, ties by increasing line_id\n\nOmitted `release` field in quote/total requests now defaults to \"2.0\" (was \"1.0\" before trial-b2v). Explicit \"1.0\" or \"2.0\" requests always get that release's behavior regardless of the current default. Response `release` field echoes the release actually used. Applies to every supplied charge set regardless of service_on dates.\n\nIf a future release changes the current default again, keep 1.0 and 2.0 behavior intact (add a new release_agreements entry / bump CURRENT_RELEASE) rather than mutating these two."
  },
  "memory_after": {
